    title: "Turn the wave into events",
    term: "Preprocessing + Level-Crossing encoding",
    text: "The signal is normalized, then a spike is produced when the waveform crosses a meaningful threshold. That gives the network a more event-focused view than sending every sample as a constant stream.",
  },
  {
    number: "03",
    title: "Choose the little building blocks",
    term: "SNN architecture",
    text: "A network of simplified neurons processes those spikes. The SLIF model keeps the neuron math lightweight, while synaptic delays give signals time to arrive in useful order.",
  },
  {
    number: "04",
    title: "Teach the model from examples",
    term: "Training",
