    <h2 id="engineering-puzzle-title" class="mt-2 font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">The real engineering puzzle</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-white/80">
      A model that fits comfortably on a laptop may be too large for a compact chip. The Digilent Basys 3 uses an Artix-7 FPGA, and the design has to work within limited on-board memory—especially <strong class="text-white">BRAM</strong>, the chip’s built-in block memory—while still learning to distinguish five heartbeat categories.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-surface p-5 sm:p-6">
